  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New module `crates/app/src/operation/feed_rating.rs`. It gives the feed that a tool states for a hole operation:\n  - the cutting-data row of the tool and the stock material, if a row is in force;\n  - else `tool.feed`.\n- A Drill operation takes that feed for `feed` and `plunge_feed`. A Thread operation takes it for `feed` and caps `plunge_feed` at it. This occurs:\n  - when the operation is created (`cutting_rows::seed_feed_for_tool`: ribbon quick-add, MCP `add_operation`, the recognizer);\n  - when the tool of the operation changes (`EditOperationLinks`, through the new `cutting_rows::retargeted_params`). Undo restores the old feeds.\n- `posting::verification_report` has a new blocking problem. If a Drill or Thread operation feeds above the feed of its tool, the post is refused. The message names the operation, the two feeds in document units and the tool. It tells the user what to change.\n  - Drill: the highest feed of the generated path. Tap cycles are not judged here, because their feed is rpm x pitch.\n  - Thread: the higher of `feed` and `plunge_feed`, stated at the cutting edge.\n- A saved project keeps its feeds on load. A project with a feed above the tool opens, and the post refuses it with the message. The project file format does not change (no version step).\n- Decision entry: `docs/decisions/2598-hole-op-tool-feed.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Cause: each new operation got the default feeds 1200 / 300 mm/min. The feed seed changed only milling kinds with a named material row. Nothing compared the feed of a hole operation with its tool. A drill was posted at F300 with a tool that states 115 mm/min.\n- Reproduction: `hole_feed_rating` failed on `origin/main` (drill at 1200/300, Thread at 1200, verify clean, post written).\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/hole_feed_rating.rs`, MCP client)\n\n- `drill_and_thread_mill_take_the_tool_feed_and_post_it`: the drill takes 115/115 from DR-0600 and the Thread takes 400 from TM-0600-P125. The Fanuc post has the drill cycle at F115. No F word is above 400.\n- `a_feed_above_the_tool_is_refused_at_the_post_by_name_and_kept_on_load`: a user feed of 1200 is accepted as an edit and is undoable. Verify names the two operations. The post is refused and writes no file. Save and open keep the feeds, and the post is still refused. Feeds at the tool's value post again.\n- `setting_a_new_tool_takes_its_feed_and_undo_restores_the_old_one`: `set_tool` to DR-0300 gives 120/120. Undo gives the old 90/80.\n\nAll 3 pass.\n\n## Fixtures and examples (second commit)\n\nThese gave a hole operation a feed above its tool. Each now states the feed of its tool:\n- tests: `lathe_workholding_kinds`, `setup_align_hole_kinds`, `stock_source_holes_support/mod.rs`, `tool_cutting_rows`, `wcs_rotation_control`, `first_router_part`.\n- `tool_cutting_rows`: the drill assertion now expects the tool feed (410/410) and not the row feed.\n\n## Golden changes\n\n- `examples/catalog/2d/first-part/first-part.nc`: 4 lines, `G83 ... Q6. F300` -> `F115` (the four holes at X+-38 Y+-23). `build.camscript` sets the Drill1 feeds to 115. The `.camproj` is rebuilt from the script.\n- `examples/first-part.nc`: 4 lines, `G73 X+-38. Y+-23. Z-1. R22. Q18. F300` -> `F115`. In `examples/first-part.camproj` only the two Drill1 feed values change.\n- `examples/first-router-part.nc`: 1 line, `G73 X53 Y50 Z-14.803 R0 Q4 F150` -> `F115`. `examples/first-router-part.camproj` is saved again from its command build (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1`, decision of #1917). Against main it differs only in: the Drill1 `feed` and `plunge_feed` (150 -> 115) and the 16 cached drill moves (`\"feed\": 150.0` -> `115.0`); the stamps of Drill1, 2D Pocket1 and 2D Contour1 (the pocket and contour stamps read the drill, so a hand edit of only the drill makes them stale); and `\"version\"` 71 -> 72 (the current `PROJECT_VERSION` on main).\n- `site/content/guide/getting-started/first-router-part.md`: the drill feed text is now 115 mm/min and the quoted G73 line has F115.\n- No CL golden and no snapshot PNG changes.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on head `e345c7145` (the branch with `origin/main` at `c41460870` merged in): 568 steps, 0 failed. The branch also merges cleanly with `origin/main` at `75e74a9cb` (`git merge-tree`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The reseed when the stock material changes (`CuttingData` / stock-material commands). They still change only the row feeds, as before.\n- Inch documents: the message uses the document units, but no test opens an inch project.\n- Tap cycles (their feed is rpm x pitch and is not judged here).\n- The GUI. The quick-add and the property panel go through the same commands, but no UI test was run for this change.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\n- #2655: a thread mill on a through hole from `detect_holes` gets a gouge report on each helix move. The pinning test uses a blind hole for this reason.\n\nChangelog: Drill and thread-mill operations now take the feed of their tool when you create them or change their tool. A feed above the tool's feed blocks the post with a message that names the operation and the tool.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #2598\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n\n\n",
